---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { profile } from "../data/site";
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Yunxi Kong's path from economics and mathematics to interactive AI systems and societal computing.">
  <header class="page-hero"><p class="page-label">About</p><h1>Why I build</h1><p class="lede">I want to understand how better machines can give people more room to think, choose, and act.</p></header>
  <article class="prose standalone-prose">
    <p>I came to these questions through economics and mathematics at Syracuse, followed by Economics and Computation at Duke. Economics gave me a way to think about choices under constraints: who has access, what incentives shape a decision, and why a useful idea may never become an available option. Building software gave me a way to ask what happens when some of those constraints can be changed.</p>
    <p>I am now a Research Assistant at UNC ACMLab, working with Prof. Guorong Wu. Across learning environments, scientific tools, and interactive worlds, I keep returning to the same distinction: a more capable system is not automatically a more capable person.</p>
    <h2>The question behind the projects</h2>
    <p>If intelligence becomes easier to access, what remains difficult? Understanding a result, deciding what matters, coordinating with other people, and obtaining the authority to act may become more important, not less. I want to study these questions together, rather than treating the technical system and its social setting as separate problems.</p>
    <p>That is the direction I hope to pursue in doctoral research: <strong>societal computing and computational social science, grounded in building human-AI systems</strong>. Social science helps me ask which mechanism matters. AI opens new possibilities. Engineering makes an idea concrete enough to use and test.</p>
    <p>The essays below develop this perspective. They are arguments and research questions, not claims that I have already answered them.</p>
    <div class="about-reading">
      <a href="/writing/the-next-bottleneck/"><img src="/assets/essays/next-bottleneck-720.webp" width="720" height="480" alt="Conceptual illustration of plans and collective action" loading="lazy" /><div><strong>The Next Bottleneck</strong><span>What becomes scarce when intelligence becomes cheaper?</span></div></a>
      <a href="/writing/human-capability/"><img src="/assets/essays/cognitive-exoskeleton-720.webp" width="720" height="480" alt="Conceptual illustration of a person directing their tools" loading="lazy" /><div><strong>The Cognitive Exoskeleton</strong><span>Support that expands a person's agency without taking over their goals.</span></div></a>
    </div>
    <p>Outside these academic projects, my education technology work in China is collected at <a href={profile.edtech}>Ingenius Prime</a>.</p>
    <p>Contact: <span class="email-text">{profile.email}</span></p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .about-reading { display: grid; gap: 0; margin: 1.6rem 0 2rem; }
  .about-reading a { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 144px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 1.2rem; align-items: center; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 1rem 0; text-decoration: none; }
  .about-reading img { width: 100%; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 3/2; }
  .about-reading strong { display: block; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .about-reading span { display: block; color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; margin-top: .25rem; }
  .about-reading a:hover strong { text-decoration: underline; }
  @media (max-width: 520px) { .about-reading a { grid-template-columns: 80px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: .8rem; } }
</style>
